<title>FRANCE: France sells 10 million Bull shares.</title>
<headline>France sells 10 million Bull shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry said on Thursday that it was selling about 10 million shares of Cie de Machines Bull to NEC, Motorola and Dai Nippon Printing for 22 francs per share.</p>
<p>France Telecom is also taking part in the operation.</p>
<p>After the sale, France Telecom, NEC and Motorola will hold 18.7 percent each of Bull and DNP will hold 5.8 percent, the ministry said.</p>
</text>
